---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Sporty — Privacy (Operational Draft)"
  description="Operational draft privacy notice for Sporty."
>
  <main class="policy-page">
    <h1>Privacy Notice (Operational Draft)</h1>
    <p>
      This page summarizes how Sporty currently handles personal data. It is an operational draft pending lawyer review.
      It is not a legal certification statement.
    </p>

    <section class="policy-callout">
      <h2>1. Who controls your data</h2>
      <p>
        Data controller (placeholder): Sporty EU entity (final legal name/address TODO).
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="policy-callout">
      <h2>2. Data categories we process</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Basic profile and measurements.</li>
        <li>Optional sports history and recommendation outputs.</li>
        <li>Sensitive health-related context in premium flows (for example injury context).</li>
        <li>Child-related profile and forecast data in guardian-mediated flows.</li>
        <li>Billing and credit metadata, plus pseudonymous billing ledger records.</li>
        <li>Operational security, deletion, and incident metadata.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="policy-callout">
      <h2>3. Processing purposes</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Deliver free and premium sport recommendations.</li>
        <li>Operate user accounts, credits, billing, and support operations.</li>
        <li>Store and manage recommendation history where applicable.</li>
        <li>Run deletion, rights-handling, and incident response workflows.</li>
        <li>Maintain de-identified learning events for adult flows as implemented.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="policy-callout">
      <h2>4. Legal-basis snapshot (draft)</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Strictly necessary operations (for example account operation, billing/accounting, core service delivery, and security operations)
          may rely on contract and/or legal-obligation basis, as applicable.
        </li>
        <li>
          Sensitive premium health-context processing requires explicit consent category
          <code>sensitive_health_processing</code>.
        </li>
        <li>
          Child forecast/premium processing requires explicit consent category
          <code>child_data_processing</code> in guardian-mediated flows.
        </li>
        <li>
          <code>basic_processing</code> is used as a user-facing consent/control gate for identifiable persistence features.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="policy-callout">
      <h2>5. Consent controls and withdrawal</h2>
      <p>
        You can manage consent categories in Account settings. You can revoke categories at any time.
        Revocation triggers scoped purge behavior for affected data classes under current runtime behavior.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><code>basic_processing</code></li>
        <li><code>sensitive_health_processing</code></li>
        <li><code>child_data_processing</code></li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="policy-callout">
      <h2>6. Minor processing (Day-1 posture)</h2>
      <p>
        Under-18 minor usage is allowed only through guardian-mediated flows. No direct child self-service onboarding is intended.
        Child analysis requires a paid guardian card transaction and explicit child-data consent before processing.
      </p>
      <p>
        Child identifiable results are not offered with an in-product retention-extension option at launch; guardians should export
        PDF copies from results pages if they need records beyond the 7-day retention window.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="policy-callout">
      <h2>7. Retention summary (launch defaults)</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Child identifiable analysis data and results (for example child forecast runs): retained for 7 days, then deleted by retention controls.</li>
        <li>Adult product recommendation/history data: retained per account operation and removed by revocation/deletion/account-closure workflows.</li>
        <li>Anonymous learning events: adult-only de-identified events retained as implemented; child anonymized event collection is disabled.</li>
        <li>Billing ledger: minimal pseudonymous records retained up to 10 years for legal/accounting reasons.</li>
        <li>Deletion and incident operational logs: retained up to 24 months target.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="policy-callout">
      <h2>8b. Child-data commercialization policy</h2>
      <p>
        Sporty does not sell, license, or otherwise monetize child-derived data, including child-derived aggregates, under current policy.
      </p>
      <p>
        Sporty also does not use child data for model-training or learning-event pipelines under current policy.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="policy-callout">
      <h2>8. Data subject rights and requests</h2>
      <p>
        You can request access, deletion, portability, objection/restriction, and correction where applicable.
        Current request handling follows our operational DSAR workflow.
      </p>
      <p>
        Request channel placeholders: privacy contact email TODO.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="policy-callout">
      <h2>9. Security and incident response</h2>
      <p>
        Sporty uses technical and operational controls designed to reduce risk, including consent gating, scoped deletion controls,
        and incident-response procedures. No system can guarantee absolute security.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="policy-callout">
      <h2>10. Vendors and transfers</h2>
      <p>
        Core vendors include Supabase, Cloudflare, Render, Stripe, and GitHub (development/operations context).
        Primary data storage region is Sweden (Stockholm, EU). Transfer and contract controls are tracked in internal compliance artifacts.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="policy-callout">
      <h2>11. Contact</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Privacy contact: TODO</li>
        <li>Security incident contact: TODO</li>
        <li>Legal contact: TODO</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <p>
      Operational draft; legal review pending.
    </p>
  </main>

  <footer class="footer">
    <div class="footer-inner">
      <div>
        <strong>Questions?</strong>
        <p class="lead-copy">Contact placeholders are currently TODO and will be finalized before broad launch.</p>
      </div>
      <small>© <span id="year">2025</span> Sporty</small>
    </div>
  </footer>

  <Fragment slot="scripts">
    <script>
      const yearEl = document.getElementById('year');
      if (yearEl) {
        yearEl.textContent = String(new Date().getFullYear());
      }
    </script>
  </Fragment>
</BaseLayout>
